  "body": "Ninth production-readiness stage, stacked on PR #56.\n\nScope is deliberately limited to **operational hardening** before final v1.0 certification.\n\nAdds:\n- exclusive scanner-owned output leases for canonical scan writers;\n- live-writer contention refusal;\n- stale same-host dead-PID lease recovery;\n- fail-closed handling for unreadable/foreign-host leases;\n- output-root symlink rejection;\n- exception-safe lease cleanup around scan and scan-manifest;\n- malformed/non-UTF-8 regression corpus;\n- catastrophic MemoryError propagation check;\n- manifest path-traversal refusal before output creation;\n- bounded synthetic large-repository degradation checks;\n- focused Linux/macOS/Windows hardening matrix on Python 3.11 and 3.13;\n- clean wheel/console-entry-point smoke validation.\n\nInherited regressions continue to cover parser/adaptor isolation, symlink containment, resource ceilings, cancellation, resume-after-budget, corrupt SQLite quarantine/rebuild, deterministic projections, package integrity, and release-query acceptance.\n\nAuthority boundary:\n- operational metadata does not become canonical evidence;\n- ordinary SCAN remains static/non-executing;\n- runtime validation remains explicitly authorized and sidecar-only;\n- resource stops remain coverage statements rather than success claims;\n- catastrophic process failures are not reclassified as parser uncertainty.\n\nExplicit non-claims:\n- no distributed or multi-host writer coordination;\n- no network-filesystem locking guarantee;\n- no universal power-loss atomicity;\n- no exhaustive parser fuzz proof;\n- no production performance SLA.\n\nFinal v1.0 certification remains the next independent roadmap stage.",
